Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('70b6a86ac0c5868d5b86701dc5ee19d54b0e0a4f19866eca5b098b80cc863b37',), event=Revised(decision='rustlanguage', at=datetime(2026, 9, 8, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The language is Rust, one of it, with rustls and never OpenSSL', body="*The language is Rust* (2026-09-08, ARCHITECTURE §8.6), and one of it: one workspace and one toolchain, pinned in the flake with every tool the box runs (`.#triage` is the operator's shell). TLS is rustls with `ring`, never OpenSSL, and one rustls in the tree: the server, `ureq` and `lettre` share the same 0.23, and `imap` takes a stream our rustls built. Every crate of the application is `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`; the two plugin guests (`app/plugin-fence`, `app/plugin-ics`) cannot be, because the glue `wit-bindgen` generates is `unsafe`. Clippy runs at `pedantic` with `-D warnings` over every target, beside `cargo fmt --check`, in the merge gate and in CI. Each crate's errors are typed (`thiserror`); `anyhow` is the binary's alone.", rationale='Decided 2026-09-08 (ARCHITECTURE §8.6), when the application was ported from Python to Rust and the Python was deleted. Restated 2026-11-20: its stored body began mid-sentence and repeated a clause, and it said missing_docs warns, which the workspace now allows.', supersedes=()))